---@field initialInterval? string Interval of the first retry. If retryBackoffCoefficient is 1.0 then it is used for all retries.
---@field backoffCoefficient? number Coefficient used to calculate the next retry interval. The next retry interval is previous interval multiplied by the coefficient. Must be 1 or larger.
---@field maximumInterval? string Maximum interval between retries. Exponential backoff leads to interval increase. This value is the cap of the increase. Default is 100x of the initial interval.
---@field maximumAttempts? number Maximum number of attempts. When exceeded the retries stop even if not expired yet. 1 disables retries. 0 means unlimited (up to the timeouts)
---@field nonRetryableErrorTypes? temporal.RetryPolicyNonRetryableErrorTypesList Non-Retryable errors types. Will stop retrying if the error type matches this list. Note that this is not a substring match, the error *type* (not message) must match exactly.

